A||||8||151 in. of love||Auto Zone||||1||
Z||000000||151 in. of love||02-12-2001||06:17 PM||||Hey guys/gals,<P>I am HAPPY! Today I bought a timing light, Fiero Manual, vacuum gauge, fuel pressure gauge, compression tester gauge, creeper, and a windshield scraper.<P>It was all for under $200. <P>I don't like the idea of Auto Zone putting the small guys with part shops out of business. They are this huge corporate being that is killing small store owners and the middle man warehouse business.<P>Yet I cannot help but to go to them for parts and supplies, because they are so cheap.<P>I was wondering what you guys think about this? Is it better? (Wal-mart dilema)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hank is Here||02-12-2001||06:30 PM||||Well I feel that Autozone is good for the average joe on the street.  It also can be good for a person who needs more than the average as well as long as they know what they need.  <BR>Example:  one sunday my father and I were worknig on his 46 Chevy ton and a half with a 216, found out the fuel pump was bad. My father though he was up the creek till he could special order one.  I went down to Advance Auto (our verson of Autozone)and asked for a 68 fuel pump from a pickup with a 292, pulled it out and it was the same.  <BR>So yes it can be good but you must know what you need.  Though there are large corportations out there killing businesses, these small comapnies would fade away anyway.  The average life of a business is less than 5 years in the USA, that includes even the old businesses like Kodak, GE, JnJ that have been around forever!!!<BR>There will always be the small local speed shops around that cater to really hard core auto guys but these are more expensive. <BR>I like getting things at Advance Auto but also I throw my business elsewhere when I need service and not just a low price.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||151 in. of love||02-12-2001||06:38 PM||||Hank.<P>I used to live out there in Altoona for a little while. (what a dive)<BR>Do you go to PSU?<BR>I went to S.College once for a party, WOW.<P>Anyway, I think that A.Z. is killing pretty established places such as NAPA and whatnot. I think that this is good for the consumer for the short run, but maybe not because of the local economy.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||02-12-2001||06:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 151 in. of love:<BR><B>Hank.<P>I used to live out there in Altoona for a little while. (what a dive)<BR>Do you go to PSU?<BR>I went to S.College once for a party, WOW.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep I am at PSU.  Yep this is a good town for parties, especially during Football weekends and in the summer for ArtsFest (a few riots occur, shame  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)<P>As for NAPA, who cares.  It is the National Auto Producers Association.   If NAPA goes out of business it will not hurt any single producer since it is just another way to market their products.  The autozones of hte world will just be selling their products instead.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT GT 87||02-12-2001||07:11 PM||||  I  HATE  NAPA !!!!!!!!       Steve||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||02-12-2001||09:47 PM||||For some general things, like wash fluid, basic car care products (I go to pro paint shops for the really good stuff), wiper blades, and such, I usually hit AutoZone or Meijers.  For parts, I have a list of places in my area that I always call around for the best price.  Somtimes autozone isnt always the best price.  For example, when I redid my e-brake cables, two of them were cheaper from Carquest, and I got the other one from autozone.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ToddAsh||02-13-2001||08:22 PM||||Have a little local parts store that is ALWAYS helpful,gets anything I need in a few hours and is priced the same as our local BIG Auto Store (Pep Boys). Like buying from the little local guy, but go to the department store for the sale items only.The parts kids don't have a clue and it seems such a shame to bother them to look something up.You have to check the #'s because they Really don't care. Todd||||reg||1
Z||000007||BN Boomer||02-13-2001||09:23 PM||||We don't have any AutoZones here in the Pacific Northwest yet, but I like NAPA. They always seem to have more parts in stock than the other auto parts stores/chains, and at competitive prices too.||||reg||14
Z||000008||2birds||02-13-2001||11:38 PM||||Call me a Capitalist Pig, but when it's my money I'm spending, I go for the bargain.  But I always keep in mind that a bargain is only a bargain if it is the right part in all respects.<P>At least the Autozone brand motor mounts actually fit, unlike some others.  And check out their price on a GT steering rack.||||reg||1
